  "createdAt" : 1720808864,
  "description" : "This dataset shows the percentage of superintendents, principals, and teachers who remain working in the same position from one year to the next from 2009 onward.\n\nThe unduplicated state total represents unique individuals who remain working in the same job classification anywhere in the state from one year to the next.\n\nAt the district level, a superintendent, principal, or teacher who moves from one school to another within the same district is still considered retained. At the school level, that individual would not be considered retained if they moved to a different school.\n\nThis dataset contains the same data that is also published on our DESE Profiles site: \n<a href=\"https://profiles.doe.mass.edu/statereport/staffingRetentionRates.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Staffing Retention Rates</a>",
